Step 1 — Define Requirements
The user provides:
Product category
Application
Aesthetic intent
Target budget
Production volume
Step 2 — Material Recommendation
MATSEL PRO processes the inputs and dynamically assigns importance to different criteria.
Application Requirements
        ↓
Dynamic Weighting
        ↓
Material Database Filtering
        ↓
Multi-Criteria Scoring
        ↓
Material Ranking
The system returns suitable material candidates along with an AI-generated engineering explanation.
Step 3 — Manufacturing
The selected material is mapped to compatible manufacturing processes.
The system considers:
Process compatibility
Surface roughness
Gloss
Dimensional capability
Manufacturing cost
Aesthetic outcome
Step 4 — Cost Estimation
The estimated unit cost considers:
Material
+
Manufacturing
+
Surface Treatment
+
Tooling
+
Overhead
Production volume is also considered to evaluate tooling amortisation.
Step 5 — Image Intelligence
The user can upload a product sketch or rendering.
Product Image
      ↓
Vision Analysis
      ↓
Material Family
      ↓
Aesthetic Intent
      ↓
Database Mapping
      ↓
Material Recommendation
Step 6 — AI-Assisted Decision
The final output combines:
Material suitability
Aesthetic requirements
Manufacturing feasibility
Cost considerations
Application requirements
This provides the designer with an integrated engineering decision-support workflow.
